= Now

I'm a sophomore, class of 2028, at #link("https://share.google/VnNzKh1lkAoL3rQwy")[Mass Tech].
There, I study #link("https://math.mit.edu/academics/undergrad/major/course18c.html")[Course 18-C], or Mathematics with Computer Science.
I'm generally interested in finding applied domains to explore using theoretical machinery in mathematics, especially #link("https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/category+theory#AbstractNonsense")[category theory], #link("https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5xLe77iTHuQ")[algebraic topology], and #link("https://homotopytypetheory.org/")[homotopy type theory].
I like working on problems where we can formally and rigorously prove things, but also in domains where those proofs genuinely advance our understanding of the world at large.
I want to work on the boundary of what's #link("https://zardini.mit.edu/Research/#:~:text=intellectually%20tractable")[intellectually tractable] and genuinely insightful.
This is a theme that motivates most of my current work and research.

